WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.752
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Isotomic Conjugate is the affine counterpart of isogonal conjugation.

2
00:00:06.752 --> 00:00:15.250
Reflecting each cevian foot of a point P across the midpoint of its side produces three new concurrent cevians meeting at the isotomic conjugate Paggers.

3
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:27.525
Because isotomic reflection acts purely on segment ratios along the sidelines, it inverts homogeneous barycentric coordinates: u, v, w maps to one over u, one over v, one over w.

4
00:00:27.525 --> 00:00:32.720
The Centroid X two is the unique interior fixed point of isotomic conjugation.

5
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:47.060
In Collection One, the Gergonne Point X seven and the Nagel Point X eight form the flagship isotomic pair: because the incircle and excircle touch points are symmetric about the side midpoints, X seven and X eight are exact isotomic conjugates.
